# Phase 3a flip (2026-07-28/29): every servarr-hosted site now has a direct
# upstream reachable from MS-01 - either the macvlan `lan` IP
# (servarr-compose runbooks/lan-macvlan.md, 10.0.71.20-99 range), a
# host-published port on 10.0.71.2 (the two VPN-netns services + the two
# dual-bound-on-127.0.0.1 groups), or an edge-local address for stacks that
# moved outright (httpbin-bun). The interim hairpin-to-servarr-caddy model
# is retired for every site below.
#
# WAF posture: `waf_off` everywhere in this section, matching CURRENT
# behavior exactly - servarr's caddy dropped its WAF entirely on 2026-07-24
# and the interim edge blocks never ran CRS against these either (see the
# comment this section replaces). Flipping upstreams and turning on WAF at
# the same time would conflate two changes; enabling `import waf` per site
# is a deliberate follow-up, one site at a time, watching wafctl for false
# positives (git LFS pushes, S3 sigv4, Subsonic/Jellyfin API clients, etc.)
#
# Dropped (dead backends, no longer serve anything): tdarr.erfi.io,
# tracearr.erfi.io, change.erfi.io, dockge.erfi.io, *.fn.erfi.io (deno-edge
# wildcard - platform stopped 2026-06+, no payload).
# =========================================================================

caddy.erfi.io {
